CLAP: size the host's event records by what we read out of them.

clap_event_header_t.size is the size of the record the host hands over, and a host
is free to use one record for every event type. Studio One (PreSonus CLAP Host
4.3.1) does: it stamps every event with the size of the largest it knows,
sizeof(clap_event_param_value_t) = 56, so a note arrives as a 56-byte
CLAP_EVENT_MIDI whose first 24 bytes are exactly the clap_event_midi_t it claims to
be. DPF compared size against the struct for equality, so in Studio One every MIDI
event was dropped and an instrument built with DPF never saw a note - while Reaper,
Bitwig and FL Studio, which size each event by its own type, worked.

The only size worth refusing is one too small to hold the event it claims to be,
which the cast that follows would read past the end of. Anything larger is read as
the prefix we know - which is also how an extended version of an event struct keeps
working. An upper bound would bound nothing, since the read is bounded by the struct
and size is used for nothing else here, and would re-create this bug for the next
host whose records are larger than today's largest event. A length that does drive
a read, the one in CLAP_EVENT_MIDI_SYSEX, needs its own bounds whenever that case is
implemented.

The note events had no size check at all, so a short record was read past its end;
they get the same one. Written as a plain `if (size < sizeof) break;` rather than
through DISTRHO_SAFE_ASSERT_UINT2_BREAK: the condition reads as what it refuses, and
a host sending malformed events no longer writes to stderr from the audio thread on
every one of them. In flushParameters() that macro's `break` left the for loop, so
one short record discarded every event after it, while the two checks above it
`continue`; it is a `continue` now.

That leaves the field that really says not to trust an event: space_id. Anything
other than CLAP_CORE_EVENT_SPACE_ID is another vendor's extension space, where the
same type ids mean something else, and the note and MIDI cases took it on trust.
Checking it once for the whole loop also subsumes the test inside
CLAP_EVENT_PARAM_VALUE, and matches what flushParameters() already did.

diff --git a/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginCLAP.cpp b/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginCLAP.cpp
index 831ace2..8d0ecf4 100644
--- a/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginCLAP.cpp
+++ b/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginCLAP.cpp
@@ -989,18 +989,29 @@ public:
                 for (uint32_t i=0; i<len; ++i)
                 {
                     const clap_event_header_t* const event = inputEvents->get(inputEvents, i);
 
+                    // another space is another vendor's extension, where the same type ids mean
+                    // something else entirely
+                    if (event->space_id != CLAP_CORE_EVENT_SPACE_ID)
+                        continue;
+
                     switch (event->type)
                     {
                     case CLAP_EVENT_NOTE_ON:
                        #if DISTRHO_PLUGIN_WANT_MIDI_INPUT
+                        // the record only has to hold the event it says it is; a larger one
+                        // (Studio One sizes every event like its largest) is read as its prefix
+                        if (event->size < sizeof(clap_event_note_t))
+                            break;
                         // BUG: even though we only report CLAP_NOTE_DIALECT_MIDI as supported, Bitwig sends us this anyway
                         addNoteEvent(reinterpret_cast<const clap_event_note_t*>(event), true);
                        #endif
                         break;
                     case CLAP_EVENT_NOTE_OFF:
                        #if DISTRHO_PLUGIN_WANT_MIDI_INPUT
+                        if (event->size < sizeof(clap_event_note_t))
+                            break;
                         // BUG: even though we only report CLAP_NOTE_DIALECT_MIDI as supported, Bitwig sends us this anyway
                         addNoteEvent(reinterpret_cast<const clap_event_note_t*>(event), false);
                        #endif
                         break;
@@ -1008,21 +1019,20 @@ public:
                     case CLAP_EVENT_NOTE_END:
                     case CLAP_EVENT_NOTE_EXPRESSION:
                         break;
                     case CLAP_EVENT_PARAM_VALUE:
-                        DISTRHO_SAFE_ASSERT_UINT2_BREAK(event->size == sizeof(clap_event_param_value_t),
-                                                        event->size, sizeof(clap_event_param_value_t));
-                        if (event->space_id == 0)
-                            setParameterValueFromEvent(reinterpret_cast<const clap_event_param_value_t*>(event));
+                        if (event->size < sizeof(clap_event_param_value_t))
+                            break;
+                        setParameterValueFromEvent(reinterpret_cast<const clap_event_param_value_t*>(event));
                         break;
                     case CLAP_EVENT_PARAM_MOD:
                     case CLAP_EVENT_PARAM_GESTURE_BEGIN:
                     case CLAP_EVENT_PARAM_GESTURE_END:
                     case CLAP_EVENT_TRANSPORT:
                         break;
                     case CLAP_EVENT_MIDI:
-                        DISTRHO_SAFE_ASSERT_UINT2_BREAK(event->size == sizeof(clap_event_midi_t),
-                                                        event->size, sizeof(clap_event_midi_t));
+                        if (event->size < sizeof(clap_event_midi_t))
+                            break;
                        #if DISTRHO_PLUGIN_WANT_MIDI_INPUT
                         addMidiEvent(reinterpret_cast<const clap_event_midi_t*>(event));
                        #endif
                         break;
@@ -1279,10 +1289,10 @@ public:
                     continue;
                 if (event->space_id != 0)
                     continue;
 
-                DISTRHO_SAFE_ASSERT_UINT2_BREAK(event->size == sizeof(clap_event_param_value_t),
-                                                event->size, sizeof(clap_event_param_value_t));
+                if (event->size < sizeof(clap_event_param_value_t))
+                    continue;
 
                 setParameterValueFromEvent(reinterpret_cast<const clap_event_param_value_t*>(event));
             }
         }
